{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.PathIntegrals","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Dihedral","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.PresentedGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeGroup.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.DirectSum.Finsupp","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.TensorProduct.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Filter.Basic"],"declarations":140,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.density","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.density","kind":"def","line":480,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L480-L480","doc":"**Density** (Part 3): the physical Hilbert space\n`𝓗_phys = lim→ V^{⊗n}` is spanned by the irreducible summands.\nEncoded as: the direct limit over `n` of the `V^{⊗n}` spaces\nadmits no element orthogonal to all summand embeddings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.summands_detected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.summands_detected","kind":"theorem","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L473-L473","doc":"For each partition `μ`, there exists a braid whose trace on the\ncorresponding Hecke-summand is non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.braid_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.braid_rep","kind":"def","line":470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L470-L470","doc":"The braid-closure map labels irreducible summands:\nfor each partition `μ` in the decomposition, there exists\na braid `β` whose closure detects `μ` — the Markov trace of the\nHecke-algebra image of `β`, restricted to the `S_μ` summand,\nis non-zero.  Encoded via the representation map `ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.consistent","kind":"theorem","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L464-L464","doc":"Consistency: the Markov trace is on the same Hecke algebra\nas the decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.markov","kind":"def","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L461-L461","doc":"Part 3: the Markov trace detects every irreducible summand. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.alexander","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.alexander","kind":"def","line":459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L459-L459","doc":"Part 2: Alexander surjectivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.decomposition","kind":"def","line":457,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L457-L457","doc":"Part 1: the q-Schur–Weyl decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete.mk","kind":"ctor","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L455-L455","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.KnotEigenbasisComplete","kind":"structure","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L438-L480","doc":"**Completeness of the knot-type eigenbasis** (Proposition 4.x).\n\nCombines semisimplicity of `H_n(q)`, Alexander surjectivity, and density\nin the physical Hilbert space to establish that knot types form a complete\neigenbasis replacing the Feynman path integral.\n\nThree parts:\n1. `H_n(q)` is semisimple at generic `q`, giving the complete\n   q-Schur–Weyl decomposition of `V^{⊗n}`.\n2. Alexander's theorem provides surjectivity of the braid-closure map.\n3. The direct limit `𝓗_phys = lim→ V^{⊗n}` is spanned by the\n   irreducible summands (density).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prf:knot-eigenbasis-complete","label":"prf:knot-eigenbasis-complete","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/knot-eigenbasis-complete-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.tr_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.tr_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L436-L436","doc":"Non-degeneracy: the trace is non-zero on each irreducible summand.\n(Encoded here as: the trace of the unit is non-zero.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.z_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.z_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L433-L433","doc":"`z ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.z","kind":"def","line":431,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L431-L431","doc":"Markov parameter `z` determined by `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.trace_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.trace_comm","kind":"theorem","line":429,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L429-L429","doc":"Trace property: `tr(ab) = tr(ba)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.tr","kind":"def","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L427-L427","doc":"The trace functional `tr : H_n(q) → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.hecke","kind":"def","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L425-L425","doc":"The Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":423,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L423-L423","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.MarkovTrace","kind":"structure","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L414-L436","doc":"**Markov trace** on the Hecke algebra tower `⋃_n H_n(q)`.\nThe unique trace satisfying the Markov property\n`tr(x σ_n^{±1}) = z^{±1} tr(x)` for `x ∈ H_n(q)`.\n\nOn each irreducible summand `S_λ`, the trace restricts to a non-zero\nscalar multiple of the character, so every summand is detected by\nsome braid closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.surjective","kind":"theorem","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L412-L412","doc":"Surjectivity: every link is the closure of some braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.closure","kind":"def","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L410-L410","doc":"Braid closure map `β ↦ β̂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.Braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.Braid","kind":"def","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L408-L408","doc":"Type of braids (union over all `B_n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.Link","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.Link","kind":"def","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L406-L406","doc":"Type of oriented links in `S³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L404-L404","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.AlexanderSurjectivity","kind":"structure","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L394-L412","doc":"**Alexander's theorem**: every oriented link in `S³` is the closure\n`β̂` of some braid `β ∈ B_n` for some `n`.\n\nThis guarantees surjectivity of the braid-closure map onto link types,\nwhich is essential for ensuring that the knot-type eigenbasis reaches\nevery irreducible summand of `V^{⊗n}`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete}` (part 2) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_length","kind":"theorem","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L392-L392","doc":"**Finiteness bound**: the partition list has at most `⌊n/2⌋ + 1`\nelements (one per two-row Young diagram of size `n`).\nRequires `partitions` to be duplicate-free; the bound is the\nexact count of 2-row diagrams (b = 0, …, ⌊n/2⌋). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.complete","kind":"theorem","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L386-L386","doc":"**Completeness**: every element of `V^{⊗n}` lies in the image of some\nsummand embedding — the direct sum spans the tensor power. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.summand_embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.summand_embed","kind":"def","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L383-L383","doc":"Embedding of each summand `V_μ ⊗ S_μ` into `V^{⊗n}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.S_irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.S_irrep","kind":"def","line":381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L381-L381","doc":"Irreducible `H_n(q)`-module for partition `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.V_irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.V_irrep","kind":"def","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L379-L379","doc":"Irreducible `SU_q(2)`-module for partition `μ` (spin `j = (μ₁−μ₂)/2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_rank","kind":"theorem","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L377-L377","doc":"Each partition has at most 2 parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions_size","kind":"theorem","line":375,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L375-L375","doc":"Each partition has size `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.partitions","kind":"def","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L373-L373","doc":"The set of partitions of `n` with at most 2 parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.tensor_power","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.tensor_power","kind":"def","line":371,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L371-L371","doc":"Type of the tensor power `V^{⊗n}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.n_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.n_eq","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L369-L369","doc":"Consistency: same `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.hecke","kind":"def","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L367-L367","doc":"The Hecke algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.n","kind":"def","line":365,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L365-L365","doc":"Number of tensor factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L363-L363","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SchurWeylDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L351-L392","doc":"**q-Schur–Weyl decomposition** of `V^{⊗n}` under the joint action\nof `SU_q(2)` and the Hecke algebra `H_n(q)`.\n\nWhen `q` is not a root of unity:\n```\nV^{⊗n} ≅ ⊕_{λ ⊢ n, at most 2 parts} V_λ ⊗ S_λ\n```\nwhere `V_λ` is the irreducible `SU_q(2)`-module of spin\n`j = (λ₁ − λ₂)/2` and `S_λ` is the irreducible `H_n(q)`-module.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete}` (part 1) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.spin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.spin","kind":"def","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L343-L349","doc":"The spin label associated to a two-row Young diagram:\n`j = (λ₁ − λ₂)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.numParts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.numParts","kind":"def","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L340-L341","doc":"The number of parts (rows) of a Young diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.size","kind":"def","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L337-L338","doc":"The size (number of boxes) of a Young diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L335-L335","doc":"Non-empty partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.nonincreasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.nonincreasing","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L333-L333","doc":"Non-increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.rows","kind":"def","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L331-L331","doc":"The partition as a list of row lengths in non-increasing order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram.mk","kind":"ctor","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L329-L329","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.YoungDiagram","kind":"structure","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L327-L335","doc":"**Partition with at most `r` parts**: Young diagrams indexing\nirreducible representations of `H_n(q)` for `SU_q(2)` (rank 1, so r = 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L324-L324","doc":"**Quadratic relation**: `Tᵢ² − (q − q⁻¹)·Tᵢ − 1 = 0`,\nequivalently `(Tᵢ − q)(Tᵢ + q⁻¹) = 0`.\nThe eigenvalues of each generator are `q` and `−q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.smul","kind":"def","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L320-L320","doc":"Scalar multiplication by `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.sub","kind":"def","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L318-L318","doc":"Subtraction in the algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.braid_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.braid_relation","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L313-L313","doc":"Braid relation: `TᵢTᵢ₊₁Tᵢ = Tᵢ₊₁TᵢTᵢ₊₁` for adjacent generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.T","kind":"def","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L311-L311","doc":"Generators `T₁, …, Tₙ₋₁` (images of Artin generators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.one","kind":"def","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L309-L309","doc":"Unit element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.mul","kind":"def","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L307-L307","doc":"Multiplication in the algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.q_not_root_of_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.q_not_root_of_unity","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L305-L305","doc":"`q` is not a root of unity (for semisimplicity).\nEncoded as: `q^k ≠ 1` for all `k ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L302-L302","doc":"`q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.q","kind":"def","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L300-L300","doc":"The deformation parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.carrier","kind":"def","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L298-L298","doc":"Carrier type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.n","kind":"def","line":296,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L296-L296","doc":"Number of strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L294-L294","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HeckeAlgebra","kind":"structure","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L286-L325","doc":"**Hecke algebra `H_n(q)`**: the quotient of the group algebra `k[B_n]`\nby the quadratic relation `(σᵢ − q)(σᵢ + q⁻¹) = 0`.\n\nWhen `q` is not a root of unity, `H_n(q)` is semisimple and isomorphic\nto `k[S_n]` as an abstract algebra (Jimbo's theorem).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:knot-eigenbasis-complete}` (part 1) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.yang_baxter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.yang_baxter","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L279-L279","doc":"**Yang–Baxter equation** on three tensor factors.\nGiven a triple `(a, b, c)`, we define:\n- `R₁₂` acts on the first two factors: `(a,b,c) ↦ (R(a,b), c)`\n- `R₂₃` acts on the last two factors:  `(a,b,c) ↦ (a, R(b,c))`\n\nThe equation asserts that `R₁₂ ∘ R₂₃ ∘ R₁₂ = R₂₃ ∘ R₁₂ ∘ R₂₃`\non all triples. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.R_right_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.R_right_inv","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L271-L271","doc":"`R ∘ R⁻¹ = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.R_left_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.R_left_inv","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L269-L269","doc":"`R⁻¹ ∘ R = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.R_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.R_inv","kind":"def","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L267-L267","doc":"R is invertible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.R","kind":"def","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L265-L265","doc":"The R-matrix acting on tensor products: `R : V ⊗ V → V ⊗ V`,\nrepresented as a map on pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.qsu2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.qsu2","kind":"def","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L262-L262","doc":"The quantum group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix.mk","kind":"ctor","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L260-L260","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.RMatrix","kind":"structure","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L254-L282","doc":"**R-matrix**: the universal R-matrix of `U_q(su(2))` furnishes a\nq-deformed braid operator whose eigenvalues govern the phase\nacquired under particle exchange.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:r-matrix-braiding}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.serre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.serre","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L251-L251","doc":"**Serre relation**: `E · F − F · E = (K − K⁻¹) / (q − q⁻¹)`.\nEncoded as: `(q − q⁻¹) · (E·F − F·E) = K − K⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_F_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_F_comm","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L248-L248","doc":"**Cartan–lowering commutation**: `K · F = q⁻² · F · K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_E_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_E_comm","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L246-L246","doc":"**Cartan–raising commutation**: `K · E = q² · E · K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_inv_K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_inv_K","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L244-L244","doc":"`K⁻¹ · K = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_K_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_K_inv","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L242-L242","doc":"`K · K⁻¹ = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.zero","kind":"def","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L240-L240","doc":"Zero element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.one","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L238-L238","doc":"Unit element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.smul","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L236-L236","doc":"Scalar multiplication by `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.neg","kind":"def","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L234-L234","doc":"Additive inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.add","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L232-L232","doc":"Addition (the carrier is an algebra). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.mul","kind":"def","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L230-L230","doc":"Multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K_inv","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L228-L228","doc":"Generator `K⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.K","kind":"def","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L226-L226","doc":"Generator `K` (Cartan element). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.F","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.F","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L224-L224","doc":"Generator `F` (lowering operator). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.E","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.E","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L222-L222","doc":"Generator `E` (raising operator). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.q_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.q_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L220-L220","doc":"`q ≠ 1` (non-classical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L218-L218","doc":"`q ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.q","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L216-L216","doc":"Deformation parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.carrier","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L214-L214","doc":"Carrier type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L212-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.QuantumSU2","kind":"structure","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L205-L252","doc":"**Quantum group `U_q(su(2))`**: the Hopf algebra with generators\n`E, F, K, K⁻¹` and relations:\n- `KE = q²EK`, `KF = q⁻²FK`\n- `EF − FE = (K − K⁻¹)/(q − q⁻¹)`\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:quantum-su2}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators.braid_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators.braid_relation","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L201-L201","doc":"`H₁` and `H₂` satisfy the braid relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators.H₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators.H₂","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L199-L199","doc":"Holonomy around second branch point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators.H₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators.H₁","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L197-L197","doc":"Holonomy around first branch point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators.mk","kind":"ctor","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L195-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.HolonomyGenerators","kind":"structure","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L187-L201","doc":"**Holonomy generators**: parallel transport of spectral modes around\nbranch points gives braid operators `H₁ = σ₁`, `H₂ = σ₂`.\n\nThe fundamental group of the trefoil-knot complement is `B₃`:\n`π₁(S³ \\ K₃,₂) ≅ ⟨H₁, H₂ | H₁H₂H₁ = H₂H₁H₂⟩`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:holonomy-trefoil}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.twistFlip_order_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.twistFlip_order_two","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L182-L185","doc":"The twist–flip composite has order 2: `(σ₁σ₂)² = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.twistFlip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.twistFlip","kind":"def","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L177-L180","doc":"The composite `σ₁σ₂` gives `(w₁, w₂, w₃, w₄) ↦ (w₃, w₄, w₁, w₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.flip_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.flip_involution","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L172-L175","doc":"The flip is an involution: `σ₂² = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.twist_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.twist_involution","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L167-L170","doc":"The twist is an involution: `σ₁² = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.flip","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L160-L165","doc":"**Flip involution** `σ₂`: `(w₁, w₂, w₃, w₄) ↦ (w₄, w₃, w₂, w₁)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:braid-twist-flip}`, equation (flip). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.twist","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L153-L158","doc":"**Twist involution** `σ₁`: `(w₁, w₂, w₃, w₄) ↦ (w₂, w₁, w₄, w₃)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:braid-twist-flip}`, equation (twist). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.instReprSpectralResolventTuple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.instReprSpectralResolventTuple","kind":"instance","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.instReprSpectralResolventTuple.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.instReprSpectralResolventTuple.repr","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.w₄","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.w₄","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.w₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.w₃","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L149-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.w₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.w₂","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L148-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.w₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.w₁","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L147-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple.mk","kind":"ctor","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SpectralResolventTuple","kind":"structure","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L142-L151","doc":"**Spectral resolvent tuple**: a 4-tuple `(w₁, w₂, w₃, w₄)` on\nwhich the braid involutions act.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:braid-twist-flip}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SO3Generators.R_beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SO3Generators.R_beta","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L138-L138","doc":"`R_β`: `π`-rotation about the `e₁`-axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SO3Generators.R_alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SO3Generators.R_alpha","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L136-L136","doc":"`R_α`: rotation by `2π/3` about the `e₃`-axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SO3Generators.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SO3Generators.mk","kind":"ctor","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L134-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SO3Generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SO3Generators","kind":"structure","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L127-L138","doc":"**`SO(3)` generators**: images of `Dic₃` generators under the\nadjoint map `SU(2) → SO(3)`.\n- `R_α` = rotation by `2π/3` about `e₃`-axis (3-cycle)\n- `R_β` = `π`-rotation about `e₁` (2-cycle)\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:so3-generators}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:so3-generators","label":"def:so3-generators","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/so3-generators.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.dihedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.dihedral","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L125-L125","doc":"Dihedral relation: `βαβ⁻¹ = α⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.beta_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.beta_squared","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L123-L123","doc":"`β² = −I`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.alpha_cubed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.alpha_cubed","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L121-L121","doc":"`α³ = −I`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.neg_I","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.neg_I","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L119-L119","doc":"Central element `−I`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.beta","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L117-L117","doc":"2-cycle generator `β`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.alpha","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.alpha","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L115-L115","doc":"3-cycle generator `α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.inv","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L113-L113","doc":"Inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.one","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L111-L111","doc":"Identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.mul","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L109-L109","doc":"Group multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.carrier","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L107-L107","doc":"Carrier type of `Dic₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators.mk","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.Dic3Generators","kind":"structure","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L96-L125","doc":"**`SU(2)` generators of `Dic₃`**: the binary dihedral group of\norder 12 inside `SU(2)`, generated by:\n- `α = exp(2π/3 · e₃)` — 3-cycle\n- `β = exp(π · e₁)` — 2-cycle\n\nRelations: `α³ = β² = −I`, `βαβ⁻¹ = α⁻¹`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:su2-generators}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SU2Basis.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SU2Basis.e","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L94-L94","doc":"The three basis elements `e₁, e₂, e₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SU2Basis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SU2Basis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SU2Basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SU2Basis","kind":"structure","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L87-L94","doc":"**`su(2)` basis element**: `eₐ = −(i/2)τₐ` where `τₐ` are Pauli\nmatrices, with Lie bracket `[eₐ, eᵦ] = εₐᵦc ec`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:su2-basis}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:su2-basis","label":"def:su2-basis","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/su2-basis.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3.sigma2_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3.sigma2_sq","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L83-L83","doc":"Involution: `σ₂² = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3.sigma1_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3.sigma1_sq","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Involution: `σ₁² = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3.toBraidGroupB3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3.toBraidGroupB3","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L79-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.SymmetricGroupS3","kind":"structure","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L73-L83","doc":"**Symmetric group `S₃`**: obtained from `B₃` by imposing `σᵢ² = id`.\n\nPresentation: `⟨s₁, s₂ | s₁² = s₂² = (s₁s₂)³ = id⟩`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:s3-group}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.braid_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.braid_relation","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Braid relation: `σ₁σ₂σ₁ = σ₂σ₁σ₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.sigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.sigma2","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Generator `σ₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.sigma1","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Generator `σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.inv","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.one","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Identity braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.mul","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Group multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.carrier","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Carrier type for braid elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PathIntegrals.BraidGroupB3","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PathIntegrals.lean#L48-L71","doc":"**Braid group `B₃`**: presented as `⟨σ₁, σ₂ | σ₁σ₂σ₁ = σ₂σ₁σ₂⟩`.\n\nThis is the fundamental group of the configuration space of 3\nunordered points in the plane, and is isomorphic to the fundamental\ngroup of the trefoil knot complement.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:braid-group}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}